(6223256, 917780, 15711, '<td valign="top">Your family aces it every time.  And to think you thought of backing off of using yourself and your kids. LOL  Way to to, Tim.  You always come out on top.</td>', 'Your family aces it every time.  And to think you thought of backing off of using yourself and your kids. LOL  Way to to, Tim.  You always come out on top.', '2010-11-15 09:33:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6223321, 918727, 96751, '<td valign="top">Hey Matt, congrats on top 20!</td>', 'Hey Matt, congrats on top 20!', '2010-11-15 10:07:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6223351, 918463, 122591, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=120893" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Korriban</a>: I actually agree. I had a hard time coming up with an idea for a title, and as I was thinking about it I was talking with a friend on Skype who mentioned this quote from Buddha: "Do not dwell in the past, do not dream of the future, concentrate the mind on the present moment". At the time I sort of liked the way it went with the three panels of the triptych, but after looking at it later I agree that it sort of forces the viewer into a certain way of thinking.<br/> <br/>I always have a hard time coming up with titles for my pictures, and I am starting to understand why so many photographers are simply calling their pictures "unnamed" or "untitled" :)<br/> <br/>I wonder if the title explains the votes of 1 and 2...</td>', ' Korriban: I actually agree. I had a hard time coming up with an idea for a title, and as I was thinking about it I was talking with a friend on Skype who mentioned this quote from Buddha: "Do not dwell in the past, do not dream of the future, concentrate the mind on the present moment". At the time I sort of liked the way it went with the three panels of the triptych, but after looking at it later I agree that it sort of forces the viewer into a certain way of thinking. I always have a hard time coming up with titles for my pictures, and I am starting to understand why so many photographers are simply calling their pictures "unnamed" or "untitled" :) I wonder if the title explains the votes of 1 and 2...', '2010-11-15 10:25:00.000000', NULL, 0),
